<title>USA: San Francisco board OKs $237 mln bonds for ballot.</title>
<headline>San Francisco board OKs $237 mln bonds for ballot.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The San Francisco Board of Supervisors on Monday voted to place three bond measures totalling $237 million on the June ballot.</p>
<p>The supervisors approved a $140 million bond for schools and community college campuses, a $49 million bond for multicultural community centres, and a $48 million bond for the San Francisco zoo.</p>
<p>The bond measures, which will appear on the June 3 ballot, will require two-thirds support of the voters to pass.</p>
</text>
